<title>SPAIN: Santander bought 2 pct of Telefonica - press.</title>
<headline>Santander bought 2 pct of Telefonica - press.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Banco Santander bought two percent of Telefonica during its recent privatisation for 61 billion pesetas, newspaper El Mundo reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Santander was not immediately available to comment.</p>
<p>Banco Bilbao Vizcaya (BBV) has around five percent of Telefonica, Catalan savings bank La Caixa has around the same percentage while banking group Argentaria has more than five percent in the firm.</p>
<p>The Spanish government recently sold its last 20.9 percent stake in the domestic telephone operator via a public placement.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
